From aaae678ec02f2a5078011f0d9a218d4d4a07fc4b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 15:44:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-138a: the Alias list skips the IO table's "#..."
 section marker row; the cause of the one lib failure corrected (0.138.0, no
 version change)

- lib/aliasedit.js ioAliases: a value starting with "#" is the table's own section marker -- HT9050's
  IO_Table.csv has ",#NEW_FROM_9050_DRAWING_20260923," (line 944) since 09-23 -- not an IO: it is no longer
  offered in the Alias list. lib test: a "#" row left out, a name twice listed once. lib 174 -> 175, all pass.
- CORRECTION of a606749 / tools 0135's message: the one lib failure was NOT "IO_Table.csv changed at 15:05".
  0.138 made the test stricter (every Alias must be an identifier; 0.133 only looked for C_OTD_Valve_On), and the
  marker row was already in the table (this morning's backup has it). The 15:05 edit was EastSun's own (C_CleanPanel
  On/Off Port/Bit swapped) -- found by the machine-integration session.
- No version bump on purpose: ES02 continues the numbering (0.139 is theirs); this is a machine-side patch of 0.138.0.
- HANDOVER.md section 5 and CHANGELOG.md say the same.
Tests: lib 175/175, probe 7/7 + tab-sheet tree 7/7, extension 207/207, panels all pass (e2e_build.ps1 not run).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
